1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,390
Welcome to NourishNest, an agentic AI household nutrition platform.

2
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:13,659
It connects everyday food decisions with explainable software: what is available, what could become dinner, and what needs buying.

3
00:00:13,659 --> 00:00:20,000
This demonstration follows a fictional family from pantry awareness to human-approved meal planning.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,875
Nine capabilities work together.

5
00:00:21,875 --> 00:00:24,688
Household profiles capture preferences and allergies.

6
00:00:24,688 --> 00:00:30,781
Nutrition provides estimates, recipes organize ingredients, and the pantry tracks stock and freshness.

7
00:00:30,781 --> 00:00:35,938
Planning brings meals into a week, while grocery preparation identifies shortages.

8
00:00:35,938 --> 00:00:38,750
Local knowledge retrieval adds cited context.

9
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:44,375
Specialist agents coordinate these services, and human approval controls the final action.

10
00:00:44,375 --> 00:00:50,000
The result is a connected workflow with clear explanations and visible boundaries.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,113
We built NourishNest in layers.

12
00:00:52,113 --> 00:00:58,028
Streamlit presents the experience, FastAPI exposes typed contracts, and application services own business operations.

13
00:00:58,028 --> 00:01:04,366
Deterministic engines calculate nutrition, convert units, scale recipes, allocate pantry quantities, and generate grocery needs.

14
00:01:04,366 --> 00:01:07,746
SQLAlchemy and Alembic manage persistence and schema evolution.

15
00:01:07,746 --> 00:01:11,549
Above those services sit bounded orchestration and local retrieval.

16
00:01:11,549 --> 00:01:16,620
This recording uses a rule-based fake provider, not a generative language model.

17
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:20,000
Optional Ollama and live USDA access are unused.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,750
Meet Maya and Daniel in the fictional Greenwood Family.

19
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:27,500
Their saved profiles include vegetarian preferences and peanut allergies.

20
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:31,250
The dashboard connects stock, upcoming meals, and shopping progress.

21
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:37,083
Nutrition estimates come from saved measurements and the versioned calculator, rather than generated prose.

22
00:01:37,083 --> 00:01:42,917
Their interest in protein is a planning aspiration, not a promise of nutritional adequacy.

23
00:01:42,917 --> 00:01:50,000
All demonstration food values are illustrative, and the application keeps individual dietary suitability subject to human review.

24
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,437
The recipe collection includes a curry, rice dishes, soup, salad, a tofu stir-fry, and an oat breakfast.

25
00:01:57,437 --> 00:02:01,812
Images provide varied serving inspiration, while saved ingredients drive calculations.

26
00:02:01,812 --> 00:02:06,625
The pantry has ten foods across refrigerator, freezer, and dry storage.

27
00:02:06,625 --> 00:02:13,188
Spinach has two separately dated lots, so quantity alone does not tell the whole story.

28
00:02:13,188 --> 00:02:19,312
Freshness signals highlight items worth checking soon, and a tofu threshold flags low stock.

29
00:02:19,312 --> 00:02:25,000
First-expiring-first-out logic uses dated inventory when calculating availability; browsing never silently consumes food.

30
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,167
In Meal Planner, recommendations explain pantry coverage and missing ingredients.

31
00:02:29,167 --> 00:02:34,167
We place two portions of lentil and tomato soup into Monday dinner.

32
00:02:34,167 --> 00:02:38,333
Changing servings changes the required ingredient quantities and calculated nutrition.

33
00:02:38,333 --> 00:02:43,750
The weekly board is session-local, so it is distinct from durable grocery records.

34
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:48,333
Preparing grocery needs combines planned portions and subtracts usable pantry availability.

35
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:55,000
These are point-in-time estimates: a plan does not reserve stock, consume ingredients, or mark anything purchased.

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,884
For local knowledge, we ask how cooked rice should be stored safely.

37
00:02:59,884 --> 00:03:05,174
An original fictional household note is ingested deterministically, hashed, and split into chunks.

38
00:03:05,174 --> 00:03:12,093
BM25 retrieves lexical candidates, reranking orders the evidence, and citations preserve the exact excerpt and source heading.

39
00:03:12,093 --> 00:03:15,349
The note deliberately supplies no authoritative storage limits.

40
00:03:15,349 --> 00:03:18,605
A separate injection exercise produces an untrusted-instructions warning.

41
00:03:18,605 --> 00:03:22,267
Retrieval respects household scope and never executes document instructions.

42
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:30,000
This foundation uses lexical retrieval, not embeddings, and neither RAG nor USDA structured food data replaces deterministic nutrition math.

43
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:40,083
Now the central agentic workflow: create five vegetarian dinners for two adults, prioritize food expiring this week, stay under thirty-five minutes, avoid

44
00:03:40,083 --> 00:03:42,375
peanuts, and show grocery shortages.

45
00:03:42,375 --> 00:03:47,875
The supervisor translates supported wording into typed intent and an execution plan.

46
00:03:47,875 --> 00:03:53,375
Pantry, recipe, and knowledge specialists gather independent evidence with safe read concurrency.

47
00:03:53,375 --> 00:03:57,958
Nutrition calculates selected-meal totals, and the grocery specialist consolidates shortages.

48
00:03:57,958 --> 00:04:03,000
Six agents operate within explicit tool permissions and a twelve-call ceiling.

49
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,333
Typed shared state carries evidence between stages, and the trace records which agent used which tool.

50
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:13,542
Unsupported requests can require clarification or refusal.

51
00:04:13,542 --> 00:04:18,583
The output is a reviewable preview, with constraints and warnings visible.

52
00:04:18,583 --> 00:04:25,000
It has not created a shopping list, reserved pantry stock, or made a purchase.

53
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:31,553
The critic checks the preview against constraints and current deterministic calculations, surfacing what remains unverifiable.

54
00:04:31,553 --> 00:04:36,796
A proposal freezes the exact list and quantities under a payload hash.

55
00:04:36,796 --> 00:04:40,728
The person reviews that payload and explicitly approves it.

56
00:04:40,728 --> 00:04:45,971
Approval alone does not create the list: execution is a separate action.

57
00:04:45,971 --> 00:04:51,214
Optimistic concurrency rejects stale versions, and transaction boundaries protect against partial writes.

58
00:04:51,214 --> 00:04:57,767
Replaying the same execution key returns the same completed result instead of creating another list.

59
00:04:57,767 --> 00:05:02,136
The audit trail links the preview, decision, and controlled execution.

60
00:05:02,136 --> 00:05:10,000
This local foundation does not authenticate the approving person's identity, and pantry stock and purchase status remain unchanged.

61
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,243
Quality evidence spans retrieval, orchestration, and controlled execution.

62
00:05:13,243 --> 00:05:18,514
Recorded evaluations cover thirty-six RAG cases, fifty-four multi-agent cases, and sixty-four approval cases.

63
00:05:18,514 --> 00:05:27,432
The last full suite recorded eight hundred sixty-four passes and one failure; that check was corrected, and twenty-four affected tests then passed.

64
00:05:27,432 --> 00:05:31,081
These are fixture results, not a blanket production guarantee.

65
00:05:31,081 --> 00:05:36,351
Request identifiers, typed contracts, rollback tests, migrations, and concurrency checks support the foundation.

66
00:05:36,351 --> 00:05:40,000
SQLite is demonstrated locally; PostgreSQL remains a deployment target.

67
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:51,429
NourishNest demonstrates how agentic AI can safely coordinate household nutrition workflows while deterministic services retain control of calculations and writes.

68
00:05:51,429 --> 00:05:58,286
It brings household context, grounded evidence, and accountable action into one experience.

69
00:05:58,286 --> 00:05:58,857
Grounded.

70
00:05:58,857 --> 00:05:59,429
Explainable.

71
00:05:59,429 --> 00:06:00,000
Human-approved.
